WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:00.900
New tonight.

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.802
Republicans want Trump to disappear.

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.337
That is the reporting from The Atlantic's

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:05.171
McKay Coppins,

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:06.606
who spoke to more than a dozen current

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:09.142
and former GOP officials and strategists.

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:11.177
But their plan to get rid of him.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.812
We'll have to hear this to believe it.

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:13.847
And I'm going to talk to McKay

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:15.482
about his reporting in just a moment,

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:16.616
because it all comes as Trump

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:17.617
ramps up his attacks

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:19.219
on his new top target.

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:21.121
The Florida governor, Ron DeSantis,

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:22.022
the man many consider

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.957
to be Trump's top threat in 20, 24

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:25.525
if he also enters the race.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:27.093
Kristen Holmes has been traveling

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.661
with Trump on his campaign stops

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.697
and she is OUTFRONT

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:32.899
Donald Trump

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.300
hitting the campaign trail

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.402
and pushing back on

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.770
criticism of his months

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:37.704
long hiatus

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:38.938
since announcing a third

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:40.640
presidential bid in November.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.441
And more angry

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:42.809
now and a more committed

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:43.977
now than I ever was.

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:44.911
The former president

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:46.980
not only taking aim at his critics,

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:49.749
but potential 2024 rivals as well.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:51.451
Specifically, Florida

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.153
Governor Ron DeSantis.

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:55.722
Ron would have pick up for me

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:57.090
when I hear you my brother.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.858
You know I consider that very disloyal.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.593
But it's not about loyalty.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:03.630
But to me, it is always one time allies.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.565
Is this Trump country or what?

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:08.868
You have only one choice.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:11.071
Ron DeSantis for Governor

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:13.873
He's going to be a great, great governor.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:14.941
Trump and to Sanders

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:15.575
now appear

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:16.342
on a possible

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:17.177
collision course

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:19.612
in a 20, 24 presidential primary.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.881
A rising star in the Republican Party,

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:24.084
DeSantis is coming off a 19 point

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:26.553
landslide reelection win in November.

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:27.153
Obviously, Ron

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:29.489
DeSantis is looking to run for president,

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:30.090
which is fine,

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:30.990
and he'll probably win

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.392
New Hampshire right now, without a doubt,

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:33.093
as the centrist

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:34.727
makes inroads with conservatives.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:35.328
Trump

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:37.397
trying to disrupt that momentum,

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:38.731
claiming the Florida governor

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:40.834
is now trying to rewrite history

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:41.668
when it comes

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:43.703
to his handling of COVID 19.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.238
There are Republican governors

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:46.806
who did not choices.

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:49.008
Florida was actually the first primary in

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:52.145
trying to rewrite history But DeSantis

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:54.147
isn't the only former Trump ally,

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:56.049
signaling they might take him on.

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:56.950
There may be somebody else

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.585
in that contest. I'd prefer more.

00:01:58.585 --> 00:01:59.986
It won't matter to the Pompeo's.

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:01.788
Who else decides to run?

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:03.256
We'll make that decision based on

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:04.791
whether we think this is our moment.

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:05.792
Can I be that later?

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.861
Yes. I think I can be that leader.

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:09.996
Yet not every potential rival

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:12.398
sparking a similar attack from Trump.

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:14.834
Nikki Haley called me the other day

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:17.003
to talk to me. Don't go for it.

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:17.704
But I said, look,

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:18.705
you know, go buy your heart

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:19.506
if you want to run.

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:20.240
As he embarks

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:21.040
on his third run

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:21.841
for the White House,

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:24.010
Trump is facing mounting legal woes

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:25.979
in calls by some Republicans

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:27.247
to move on from lies

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:29.516
about his 2020 election laws

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:31.584
that incited the attack on the U.S.

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:32.318
Capitol.

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.420
On the trail in South Carolina.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.689
Trump offering a different message.

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:39.058
This campaign will be about the future.

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:41.094
This campaign will be about issues.

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:41.694
Still,

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.396
the former president making clear

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:45.565
he was ready for a nominating fight,

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:48.234
even as he remains the lone GOP candidate

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:49.235
in the field.

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.170
For the moment,

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.738
we don't do prevent defense.

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:53.606
We just keep defending

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:54.374
and we're going to win and

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:55.408
we're going to win very big.

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:57.644
And Aaron, as you noted,

00:02:57.644 --> 00:02:59.145
I was with Trump this week

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:00.680
and traveled with him from New Hampshire

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:01.981
to South Carolina.

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:02.882
And it was really

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:04.717
his official campaign launch.

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:06.753
And it was interesting to see him

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:07.954
almost participating

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:09.122
in a traditional campaign,

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:10.089
something we haven't seen

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:12.525
since early 2016. He stayed on script.

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.260
He stayed away from the 20,

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.396
20 election lies for the most part.

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:17.497
He even participated

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:18.932
in a small campaign stop.

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:19.766
As we see politicians

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:21.568
do it, an ice cream and hamburger

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:22.869
shop in South Carolina

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:24.304
talking to voters

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:25.071
and his advisers

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:26.239
were absolutely thrilled.

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:28.141
He followed their advice.

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.542
But many of them that I talked to

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:30.510
they said

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:31.978
there's still some concern

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:32.779
that they don't know

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:34.581
how long this is going to last.

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:36.115
They have some concerns.

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:37.317
They believe this is how he could

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:39.319
actually reintroduce himself to voters

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:40.620
But will he stick with that?

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.921
We know Donald Trump likes to do

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:43.389
what Donald Trump likes to do.

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:44.157
Yeah, absolutely.

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:44.691
All right, Christine,

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:46.259
thank you very much for your reporting.

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:47.827
And now I want to go to McKay Coppins,

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:49.329
who wrote that story for The Atlantic

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:50.530
that I just told you about,

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:51.397
titled Republicans.

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:54.300
28, 24 Magical Thinking.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.368
What an appropriate title,

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:56.603
McKay, given what you write about.

00:03:56.603 --> 00:03:56.869
Okay.

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:58.037
So what you write about

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.172
is that virtually everyone

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:00.173
in the Republican Party

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:02.742
and you talk to dozens of people,

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:04.177
senior officials, strategists

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:06.246
and members of GOP agree

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:06.713
that it's time

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:08.248
to move on from Donald Trump.

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:08.748
But you say

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:10.850
they have no plan on toppling him.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.052
They are just hoping he goes away.

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:13.686
I mean, are

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:15.355
they just hoping he gets indicted

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:16.889
and that just magically makes

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:17.624
him disappear?

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:20.660
Well, literally, yes.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:21.828
That was one of the scenarios

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:23.162
that I heard repeatedly.

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:26.432
It was striking how consistently

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:27.767
I heard

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.435
the party needs to move on from Trump.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:30.303
We need to find a way

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:31.471
to get rid of Trump,

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:32.872
that we're way better off with Trump.

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:34.040
But then when I would ask, okay,

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.875
what's the plan for that to happen?

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:36.809
It would immediately

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.578
move into hypotheticals

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:39.812
maybe he'll get indicted

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:41.848
and his legal problems will subsume

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:44.917
and maybe he'll get bored and drop out.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:46.986
Maybe he'll lose his attention.

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:48.154
Some people,

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:48.454
you know,

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:51.124
clung to this long held delusion

00:04:51.124 --> 00:04:52.525
that maybe he would

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:53.793
become a different person

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:55.161
and now graciously

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:56.829
and make room for the next generation

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:58.231
of Republican leaders.

00:04:58.231 --> 00:04:59.766
Contrary to everything we know.

00:04:59.766 --> 00:05:01.301
What the consistent Through-line

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:02.001
was, though,

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:02.835
was that

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:04.037
they all wanted him gone,

00:05:04.037 --> 00:05:05.872
but nobody wanted to confront him

00:05:05.872 --> 00:05:06.572
directly.

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.341
There is just this fear

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:10.576
that if they if they go after him

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:12.712
or if they try to rally around

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:14.080
somebody else,

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.549
they'll spark a backlash from his base.

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:17.150
And so

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.151
everybody has kind of

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:19.319
waiting on the sidelines

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:21.321
just hoping something will change. Okay.

00:05:21.321 --> 00:05:22.889
And then there's this this

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:24.390
this hope, this morbid hope.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:25.958
But I mean, this just brings home

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:26.559
your reporting,

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:28.061
talking about magical thinking.

00:05:28.061 --> 00:05:30.663
You write this quote In my conversations

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:31.331
with Republicans,

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:32.432
I heard repeatedly

00:05:32.432 --> 00:05:33.900
that the least disruptive path

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.101
to getting rid of Trump, grim

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:36.002
as it sounds,

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:37.370
might need to be to wait

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:39.272
for his expiration.

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:41.107
There rationale was straightforward.

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:42.675
The former president is 76 years

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:43.609
old, overweight,

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:44.911
appears to maintain the diet

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:46.045
of a college freshman

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:47.080
and believes, contrary

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:47.947
to all known science,

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:49.682
that exercise is bad for you.

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:51.351
Why risk alienating his supporters

00:05:51.351 --> 00:05:53.252
when nature will take its course

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:54.887
sooner or later?

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:55.655
Okay.

00:05:55.655 --> 00:05:57.156
Obviously, this isn't just war

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:58.257
but it also is, in fact, by

00:05:58.257 --> 00:05:58.991
what we know is

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:00.460
health is reportedly fine.

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:01.327
Could easily do

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:02.462
another term as president,

00:06:02.462 --> 00:06:04.063
which is all he would be allowed to do

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:04.597
by law

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:05.231
and that there are

00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:06.999
some just sitting around hoping for

00:06:06.999 --> 00:06:07.934
that literally.

00:06:09.335 --> 00:06:09.635
Yeah.

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:10.136
I mean,

00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:10.903
we should also note

00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:12.138
that his parents

00:06:12.138 --> 00:06:13.539
both lived in their late

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:15.541
eighties or early nineties.

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:16.008
You know,

00:06:16.008 --> 00:06:18.211
one former Republican congressman

00:06:18.211 --> 00:06:19.712
described this strategy to me

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:21.714
as actuarial arbitrage.

00:06:22.382 --> 00:06:23.883
And literally said

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:26.319
that he had spoken to many Republicans

00:06:26.319 --> 00:06:27.086
who will

00:06:27.086 --> 00:06:27.820
put on the Red

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.422
Hat and campaign for Trump

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:30.923
and go up on stage with them.

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:32.291
And then the next day

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:34.460
say, I can't wait for this guy to die.

00:06:34.494 --> 00:06:35.795
That's a direct quote.

00:06:35.795 --> 00:06:37.397
And so I was taken aback

00:06:37.397 --> 00:06:39.465
by how often I heard this.

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:40.199
I thought it was

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:42.468
kind of a morbid, dark joke at first,

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:44.203
but I heard it so often

00:06:44.203 --> 00:06:45.571
that it started to become clear

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:47.073
that this was actually

00:06:47.073 --> 00:06:48.508
what a lot of Republicans believe.

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:49.142
And it just speaks

00:06:49.142 --> 00:06:51.043
to the desperate desperation in the party

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:52.845
right now. It absolutely does.

00:06:52.845 --> 00:06:53.079
All right.

00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:54.414
Thank you very much, Mike.

00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:54.981
I appreciate it.

00:06:54.981 --> 00:06:55.581
Hope everyone will read

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:56.649
your full article in The Atlantic.

00:06:56.649 --> 00:06:57.049
Thanks.

00:06:58.184 --> 00:06:58.651
Thank you.

